; how much light a material blocks. opaque → translucent → transparent.
; opaque: metals (free electrons absorb photons), stone, wood.
; transparent: glass, water, air (photon energy below bandgap).
; refraction index: water 1.33, glass 1.5, diamond 2.42.
; in 3d/pratibimba: alpha (0=transparent, 1=opaque), roughness, refraction.

(kosha opacity
  (vishesa common-sense-varga materials-varga)
  (swarupa subanta)
  (yukta photon pbr domain-3d))
